 Error. So the pod exists, but when trying to get logs, it\'s not found. That could happen if the pod was deleted after the get pods command. Alternatively, maybe the pod is still in a crash loop and the logs are not accessible. Or perhaps the user needs to use a different command, like kubectl describe pod to get more details. Alternatively, check the events for the pod to see why it\'s in an error state. But the user\'s last attempt was to get logs, which failed. So maybe the next step is to describe the pod to get more information about why it\'s in an error state. So the tool call should be to exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd with the command "kubectl describe pod profile-5889bcfdc5-c5q28 -n hotel-reservation" to get detailed info about the pod\'s status, events, and any errors.\n</think>\n\n', additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl describe pod profile-5889bcfdc5-c5q28 -n hotel-reservation"}', 'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-b489b6a1650e1aff', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 579, 'prompt_tokens': 4319, 'total_tokens': 4898, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfe0f-47e6-77b2-a825-21443a18a04b-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl describe pod profile-5889bcfdc5-c5q28 -n hotel-reservation'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-b489b6a1650e1aff', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 4319, 'output_tokens': 579, 'total_tokens': 4898}), ToolMessage(content='Name:             profile-5889bcfdc5-c5q28\nNamespace:        hotel-reservation\nPriority:         0\nService Account:  default\nNode:             node0.htliang2-agent.insai-pg0.apt.emulab.net/128.110.9