ed 5m20s ago. So maybe the PVC wasn\'t available at the time of scheduling. But now it\'s Bound. However, the pod is already running. Wait, the pod\'s status is Running, so maybe the PVC is now available. But why did the pod start even though the PVC wasn\'t there initially? Maybe the pod was scheduled after the PVC was created. \n\nBut the main issue is that the `profile` pod is crashing. The `profile` pod\'s container is crashing with exit code 2. The logs for `profile` pod show that the container started and then failed. The exit code 2 might indicate a specific error. \n\nWait, the `profile` pod\'s container is using the image `yinfangchen/hotelreservation:latest`. Maybe the application inside that container is failing because it can\'t connect to the MongoDB database. Even though the `mongodb-profile` pod is running, maybe there\'s a network issue or the MongoDB service isn\'t accessible. \n\nAlternatively, the `profile` pod might be trying to connect to a database that\'s not properly configured. For example, if the MongoDB service is not reachable due to a misconfigured service or network policy. \n\nAnother angle: the `profile` pod\'s logs might have more details. Earlier attempts to get logs for the `profile` pod resulted in an error because the pod wasn\'t found, but now the pod is listed as Running. Wait, the `profile` pod is `profile-5889bcfdc5-c5q28` and is in the Running state but with the container in CrashLoopBackOff. \n\nSo, the next step is to check the logs of the `profile` pod to see the exact error message. The exit code 2 might be a generic error, but the logs could clarify if it\'s a connection issue to MongoDB, a configuration error, or something else. \n\nTherefore, the next tool call should be to get the logs of the `profile` pod to identify the root cause of the crash. If the logs show that the application can\'t connect to MongoDB, then the issue might be with the MongoDB service\'s availability or configuration. If the logs show a different error, that would point to another problem.\n</think>\n\n', additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl logs profile-5889bcfdc5-c5q28 -n hotel-reservation"}', 'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-a5e632034d633563', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 939, 'prompt_tokens': 8327, 'total_tokens': 9266, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfe10-eb05-7a70-8064-feb6a6ceea3d-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl logs profile-5889bcfdc5-c5q28 -n hotel-reservation'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-a5e632034d633563', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 8327, 'output_tokens': 939, 'total_tokens': 9266}), ToolMessage(content='{"level":"info","time":"2026-03-17T23:10:07Z","message":"TLS disabled."}\n{"level":"info","time":"2026-03-17T23:10:07Z","message":"Set global log level: info"}\n{"level":"info","time":"2026-03-17T23:10:07Z","message":"Tune: setGCPercent to 100"}\n\x1b[90m2026-03-17T23:10:07Z\x1b[0m \x1b[32mINF\x1b[0m \x1b[1mcmd/profile/main.go:24\x1b[0m\x1b[36m >\x1b[0m \x1b[1mReading config...\x1b[0m\n\x1b[90m2026-03-17T23:10:07Z\x1b[0m \x1b[32mINF\x1b[0m \x1b[1mcmd/profile/main.go:37\x1b[0m\x1b[36m >\x1b[0m \x1b[1mRead database URL: mongodb-profile:27017\x1b[0m\n\x1b[90m2026-03-17T23:10:07Z\x1b[0m \x1b[32mINF\x1b[0m \x1b[1mcmd/profile/main.go:38\x1b[0m\x1b[36m >\x1b[0m \x1b[1mInitializing DB connection...\x1b[0m\n\x1b[90m2026-03-17T23:10:18Z\x1b[0m \x1b[31mPNC\x1b[0m \x1b[1mcmd/profile/db.go:33\x1b[0m\x1b[36m >\x1b[0m \x1b[1mno reachable servers\x1b[0m\npanic: no reachable servers\n\ngoroutine 1 [running]:\ngithub.com/rs/zerolog.(*Logger).Panic.func1({0x970d7