 clear, the next step would be to adjust either the service's selector or the pod's labels to ensure they match, allowing the service to correctly route traffic to the pod.\n</think>\n\n**Tool Choice**: `exec_kubectl_cmd_safely`  \n**Command**: `kubectl -n hotel-reservation get pod mongodb-profile-775dfd4bd7-zqlqh -o yaml`  \n\n**Rationale**: The `mongodb-profile` service has no endpoints, but the pod `mongodb-profile-775dfd4bd7-zqlqh` is listed as `Running`. To diagnose why the service isn't detecting the pod, I need to inspect the pod's metadata (specifically its labels) to confirm whether the service's selector (`io.kompose.service=mongodb-profile`) matches the pod's labels. A mismatch here would explain why the service has no endpoints and the `profile` service cannot connect to MongoDB. This step is critical to identifying the root cause of the misconfiguration.", additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': Usage(completion_tokens=557, prompt_tokens=3892, total_tokens=4449, completion_tokens_details=None, prompt_tokens_details=None), 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfe13-100e-7413-87d8-c294f69675e5-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 3892, 'output_tokens': 557, 'total_tokens': 4449}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='465f063b-867c-45fa-92fb-e81e23444a14')]]
