ing. However, the available tools don't include checking network policies directly. \n\nWait, the user has the 'get_network_policy' tool? No, looking back, the available tools don't include that. The user can only use the listed functions. So the next step is to check the endpoints again, maybe after waiting. If the endpoints still don't show up, then there's a deeper issue. But given the information, the user should proceed to check the endpoints again to confirm.\n</think>\n\n", additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl -n hotel-reservation get endpoints mongodb-profile"}', 'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-825a9f92dec51a14', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 824, 'prompt_tokens': 12126, 'total_tokens': 12950, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfe14-14f3-73a0-9df9-d4c35eab6acf-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl -n hotel-reservation get endpoints mongodb-profile'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-825a9f92dec51a14', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 12126, 'output_tokens': 824, 'total_tokens': 12950}), ToolMessage(content='NAME              ENDPOINTS           AGE\nmongodb-profile   10.244.0.29:27017   9m33s\n', id='bc19dfc8-7e2b-4d12-b11c-a5b897129f05', tool_call_id='chatcmpl-tool-825a9f92dec51a14'), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='2345233c-5056-4b63-864a-49d04d24810d'), AIMessage(content="<think>\nOkay, let me try to figure out what's going on here. The user is dealing with a hotel reservation application where t