e are no more actions to rollback, the next step is probably to check if the system is back to its initial state. But the user\'s goal is to rollback all changes, and they might need to confirm that everything is restored. However, the tools available don\'t include a way to check the system\'s state directly. \n\nWait, the r_submit_tool is described as the tool to submit after rolling back all changes. Since the rollback_command has already undone all possible actions, the system should be back to the initial state. Therefore, the correct next step is to use the r_submit_tool to signal that the task is complete. \n\nUsing the submit_tool would end the process. The user mentioned that if they call submit_tool, the process ends immediately. So, after ensuring all rollbacks are done, they should submit the result. \n\nTherefore, the right choice is r_submit_tool. There\'s no need to call any other tool because there are no more commands to rollback, and the task is complete.\n</think>\n\nr_submit_tool\n\nThe r_submit_tool is necessary to formally conclude the rollback process once all reversible actions have been undone. Since the rollback_command indicated "No more actions to rollback," it confirms that the system has been restored to its initial state. Submitting at this stage ensures the task is marked as complete and prevents further unnecessary operations. This tool is specifically designed for final submission after successful rollback, aligning with the process\'s requirements. \n\n<tool_call>\n{"name": "r_submit_tool", "arguments": {}}\n</tool_call>', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': Usage(completion_tokens=445, prompt_tokens=962, total_tokens=1407, completion_tokens_details=None, prompt_tokens_details=None), 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfe16-2def-7430-ab51-74da53053cb0-0', 