reattempt the deployment.  \n```python\nsubmit_tool(ans={"namespace_missing": True, "permissions_denied": True})\n```', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 384, 'prompt_tokens': 5054, 'total_tokens': 5438, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfe18-1cfb-77f0-95c5-9c13cab67df9-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 5054, 'output_tokens': 384, 'total_tokens': 5438}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='cd491f27-6c91-4709-b909-3e06254a4c1b'), AIMessage(content="<think>\nOkay, let me try to figure out what's going on here. The user is trying to fix an issue with their hotel reservation application where the 'profile' service can't connect to 'mongodb-profile'. They've gone through several steps, checking services, pods, and namespaces. \n\nFirst, they tried to describe the 'mongodb-profile' service but got a 'Not Found' error. Then they checked the list of services in the 'hotel-reservation' namespace and found that the namespace itself wasn't there. When they tried to create the namespace, they got a permission error. Now, they're stuck because the system is in a 'tearing_down' state and they can't submit any more answers.\n\nThe main problem seems to be the missing namespace. Without the 'hotel-reservation' namespace, all the services and deployments related to the application can't exist. The user doesn't have the necessary permissions to create the namespace, so they can't proceed on their own. \n\nSince the system won't allow further submissions, the best course of action is to inform the user that they need to contact the cluster administrator. The administrator can create 