ation` namespace and lack of cluster permissions. No additional tools can resolve this without administrative access. \n\n**Final Answer:**  \nThe `hotel-reservation` namespace is missing, and the user lacks cluster-level permissions to create it. Contact the cluster administrator to create the namespace and reattempt the deployment.  \n```python\nsubmit_tool(ans={"namespace_missing": True, "permissions_denied": True})\n```', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 394, 'prompt_tokens': 4833, 'total_tokens': 5227, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfe17-f8e4-78a0-96f3-eb0a6759f000-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 4833, 'output_tokens': 394, 'total_tokens': 5227}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='9efce4a8-25c5-40a6-8213-20bb111cc8c6'), AIMessage(content="<think>\nOkay, let me try to figure out what's going on here. The user is trying to fix an issue with their Kubernetes cluster where the 'hotel-reservation' namespace is missing, and they don't have the necessary permissions to create it. They've already tried several steps, like checking services and deployments, but kept getting errors because the namespace didn't exist.\n\nFirst, they tried using 'kubectl get services' and 'kubectl describe service' but got 'NotFound' errors because the namespace wasn't there. Then, when they tried to create the namespace with 'kubectl create namespace', they got a 'Forbidden' error, indicating they don't have the right permissions at the cluster level. \n\nNow, the user is in a loop where every attempt to submit an answer is failing because the system is in a 'tearing_down' state.