 exec_kubectl_cmd_safely\n\ntool description: This is a tool used to safely execute kubectl commands. Whatever commands you executed will be stored in a rollback mechanism which later is used to roll back the cluster state in case your current attempt fails.\n\n    Args:\n        command (str): The kubectl command you would like to execute, must start with "kubectl"\n        INTERACTIVE COMMANDS ARE NOT SUPPORTED, e.g. "kubectl edit" \n        INTERACTIVE FLAGS ARE NOT SUPPORTED, e.g., "kubectl logs -f"\n\nJustification: The `hotel-reservation` namespace is missing, which is critical because all services (e.g., `profile`, `mongodb-profile`) are supposed to reside in this namespace. Running `kubectl get namespaces` will confirm the absence of the namespace and help identify if this is the root cause of the missing services and misconfigured deployments.', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 529, 'prompt_tokens': 4056, 'total_tokens': 4585, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfe17-834e-7491-b350-ab17357a570e-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 4056, 'output_tokens': 529, 'total_tokens': 4585}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='03c308a3-dc71-4acf-973c-ce6789ef26e3'), AIMessage(content="<think>\nOkay, let's try to figure out what's going on here. The user is trying to troubleshoot an issue with their hotel reservation application. The main problem seems to be that the 'profile' service can't connect to 'mongodb-profile', leading to crashes. \n\nFirst, the LLM checked the 'mongodb-profile' service using 'get_services' and found it wasn't there. Then, they tried to describe the service with 'kubectl describe service mongodb-profile', but it wasn't found. Next, they checked the list of services in the 'hotel-reservation' namespace with 'kubectl get services -n hotel-reservation', which also didn't show the service. \n\nThen, when trying to describe the 'profile' service, there was an error about the namespace not existing. The LLM then checked the namespace with 'kubectl get namespace hotel-reservation' and found it missing. This suggests that the namespace 'hotel-reservation' hasn't been created, which is why all the services are missing.\n\nSo, the root cause is the absence of the 'hotel-reservation' namespace. Without this namespace, the services like 'profile' and 'mongodb-profile' can't be properly deployed or accessed. The next step should be to create the missing namespace. Once the namespace is created, the services can be deployed into it, and the 'profile' service should be able to connect to 'mongodb-profile' correctly. \n\nThe LLM needs to use the 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely' tool to create the namespace. The command would be 'kubectl create namespace hotel-reservation'. After creating the namespace, they should verify its existence with 'kubectl get namespace hotel-reservation' to ensure it's successfully created. Then, they can proceed to check the services again to confirm they're present and properly configured.\n</think>\n\n", additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl create namespace hotel-reservation"}', 'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-95dafcd3f7e0874a', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 400, 'prompt_tokens': 5264, 'total_tokens': 5664, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfe17-9c23