eck the Kubernetes resources, but they keep running into errors.\n\nFirst, they tried checking the 'mongodb-profile' service using 'kubectl describe', but it wasn't found. Then they checked the list of services and confirmed that 'mongodb-profile' wasn't there. Next, they tried looking into the 'profile' service's configuration, but the namespace 'hotel-reservation' wasn't found either. \n\nWhen they tried to create the namespace, they got a permission error, indicating they don't have the necessary rights. The system is now in a 'tearing_down' state, which is preventing any further actions. The user has tried submitting the answer multiple times but keeps getting the same error.\n\nThe root cause seems to be the missing namespace and lack of permissions. Since the user can't create the namespace themselves, the only solution is to contact the cluster administrator. They need to create the 'hotel-reservation' namespace manually and then reattempt the deployment. Without that namespace, the services can't be properly set up, leading to the connection issues.\n\nSo, the final answer should clearly state that the namespace is missing and the user doesn't have the required permissions. They need to reach out to the admin to resolve this. Even though the system is in a tearing down state, the answer has to be submitted as per the instructions.\n</think>\n\n", additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"ans": "{\\"namespace_missing\\": true, \\"permissions_denied\\": true}"}', 'name': 'submit_tool'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-8991aaf6555c635d', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 351, 'prompt_tokens': 7559, 'total_tokens': 7910, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfe19-0f96-7f40-8b22-4